  "body": "Stacked on #2964. Review the [reentrant punch changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/4915595814341646b6d5e26160084754c5467b36...6201b325cd26be81c9938e7b485124af42864ccf).\n\nCompare the top and bottom faces of the complete prism. Verify its walls and the selected profile. Allow a reentrant corner when the actual rough wire can reach it within tolerance. Check the nearest unrelated face and stock limit before writing any file.\n\nThe synthetic example has a 1 mm deep notch with two sloped sides. The offline Agie Control plotted all seven faces through the rough cut and three trims. Measured wire offsets were 0.245, 0.155, 0.140 and 0.134 mm. At X zero, the four notch tips measured Y 9.246222, 9.155773, 9.140698 and 9.134668 mm. Each agrees with the nominal slopes and the wire offset. The plot kept the 1 mm separation and returned to the threading hole.\n\nThe independent gate passed all 89 post library tests, 11 native app tests and both prism geometry tests. Strict Clippy passed for the app, post and geometry libraries. The controller formal check had zero job errors. It requested machining and reference values and reported option 131072.\n\nRun the synthetic job from the repository root with `cargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/notched-punch.camscript`. No physical cut was made.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native Agie post accepts a vertical punch with checked reentrant corners and refuses features the rough wire cannot reach safely.\n\nFixes #2956\n",
